{"id": "unknown-2026-09-02-016", "date": "2026-09-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["food_safety"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "New Zealand and French studies call attention to Campylobacter", "content": "<p>A study in New Zealand has provided an insight into Campylobacter contamination and antimicrobial resistance in fresh chicken.</p><p>Campylobacter&#xA0;was detected in 50 percent of 24 samples. Among confirmed isolates, there were high levels of resistance to tetracycline and ciprofloxacin, while the majority were susceptible to erythromycin.</p>", "sources": [{"name": "food_safety_news", "url": "https://www.foodsafetynews.com/2026/09/small-new-zealand-study-calls-attention-to-campylobacter-in-chicken/", "type": "rss"}]}
